@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title Tutorial 2 · Borrow timing: synthetic Label and its Card owner
hide footbox
$caller(caller, "Caller\nUses the returned Label")
$callee(getter, "current_label\nBorrows Card for the call")
$owner(card, "Card\nOwns its current Label")
== Case 1: refresh ends the borrow before owner destruction ==
caller --> getter : Entry: lend Card; valid($card, call)
activate getter
getter --> caller : Return: lend Label in owner($card)
deactivate getter
note over caller, card : Caller may use this Label while Card lives and refresh has not begun.
card ->x caller : refresh_card entry: invalidate this Label borrow
note over caller, card
  Card remains alive; this old Label is unusable.
  After refresh, current_label can lend the new Label.
end note
== Case 2: no refresh before Card destruction ==
caller --> getter : Entry: lend Card; valid($card, call)
activate getter
getter --> caller : Return: lend Label in owner($card)
deactivate getter
note over caller, card : Caller may use this Label while Card lives.
card ->x caller : Card destruction: end owner region and Label borrow
legend bottom
  Time runs downward within each separate case; spacing is not duration.
  Actor = caller; rectangle = callee; circle on base = owner; bar = active call.
  Dashed arrow = borrowed access; marked end = invalidation, not caller destruction.
  Neither borrow gives the caller permission to destroy_label.
  Non-normative: C1, C3, C5. Synthetic lending subset; access paths omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
